sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/thompson1917-ch03-07> dct:description "Proof scope of the kernel-checked statement recorded as thompson1917-ch03-07: 2 statement(s) the Lean kernel checked and 3 assumption(s) stated in the module header and not proved. The source's claim (\"Weight tends to vary as the cube of linear dimensions during growth\", On Growth and Form 1917) is what the statement was written FROM, not what was checked." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: If W L = k L^3 for all L > 0 with k > 0, then for L1 ≠ L2 the log-log slope (log W L2 − log W L1)/(log L2 − log L1) equals exactly 3 (cubeLaw_loglog_exponent) and W L2 / W L1 = (L2/L1)^3 (cubeLaw_ratio)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Kernel-checked: Contrapositive: two sizes with a log-log slope b ≠ 3 rule out W = k L^3 for every k (not_cubeLaw_of_exponent_ne_three)." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: A single linear dimension L and mass W of one body family; fixed shape and constant density are what W = k L^3 encodes." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: Thompson's \"mainly (though not wholly)\" is not formalised: the theorem is exact, the law is approximate, and the tolerance band [2.5, 3.5] the claim test uses is a decision rule outside the module." ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: No data enters the module; the measured exponents are read from the claims thread's result files and pointed to." ;
    rdfs:comment "The kernel-checked statements are theorems of the model; the assumptions are the model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: A single linear dimension L and mass W of one body family; fixed shape and constant density are what W = k L^3 encodes; Thompson's \"mainly (though not wholly)\" is not formalised: the theorem is exact, the law is approximate, and the tolerance band [2.5, 3.5] the claim test uses is a decision rule outside the module; No data enters the module; the measured exponents are read from the claims thread's result files and pointed to. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Thompson.lean> .
}

sub:provenance {
  sub:assertion prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-lean-thread-builder> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Thompson.lean> , <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-lean-thread-builder> a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "delphisci lean thread (Claude Fable 5.1 writing the Lean modules and this builder; the Lean kernel, not the model, checked the proofs)" ;
    delphi:usesModel <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a delphi:LanguageModel ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1" ;
    dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" .
}

